  "page1": {
    "title": "Hands That Help Others",
    "subtitle": "How small acts of service and sharing make a whole community stronger.",
    "body": "Mr. Han lives alone next door. Last week his lights went dark, and he could not climb the stairs.\n\nMina and her brother carried his bags up each day. They never asked for money. This is what we call service: helping with no reward.\n\nSharing is also a kind of service. When we share food, time, or kind words, someone's day gets better.\n\nSmall acts can <mark>build a community</mark> that feels like family. A lonely neighbor starts to smile again. People who once received help often help others later.\n\nSo kindness spreads, like a warm light passing between homes. You do not need to be rich or grown up. A child can carry a bag or read aloud. When many hands help, a whole town grows stronger.",
    "illustration": "assets/illustrations/venus/2026-07/19.jpg",
    "illustration_caption": "Two kids carry a neighbor's bags up the stairs while others share food and smiles."
  },
